// Virtual filesystem - imports WASI filesystem interfaces for custom implementation
//
// IMPORTANT: the `wasi:*` package versions in `wit/deps` must match the
// versions that `wasmtime-wasi` ships in `src/p2/wit/deps` for the wasmtime
// release we depend on. Our bindings are registered in the linker *after*
// `wasmtime_wasi::p2::add_to_linker_async` in order to shadow its filesystem
// implementation, and the linker only treats them as the same entry when the
// interface names — version suffix included — match exactly.
//
// If the versions drift, both implementations end up registered side by side.
// Guests import `wasi:filesystem/types@0.2.0` (the version baked into the
// preview1 adapter), which wasmtime resolves through its semver-compatible
// lookup table, and that table keeps the *highest* version registered on the
// `0.2` track. wasmtime-wasi always wins that race, so the VFS is silently
// bypassed: mounts and volumes disappear and every path under them returns
// ENOENT. `linker_shadows_wasmtime_wasi_filesystem` in `src/linker.rs` guards
// against this.
package eryx:vfs;

world virtual-filesystem {
  import wasi:filesystem/types@0.2.12;
  import wasi:filesystem/preopens@0.2.12;
}
